'''''Trifolium medium''''', the '''zigzag clover''',<ref>{{PLANTS|id=TRME|taxon=Trifolium medium|accessdate=15 December 2015}}</ref> is a [[flowering plant]] species in the bean family [[Fabaceae]]. It is similar in appearance to red clover, ''[[Trifolium pratense]]'', but the leaflets are narrower and have no white markings and the narrow stipules are not bristle-pointed.<ref name="Blamey">{{cite book|last1=Blamey|first1=M.|last2=Fitter|first2=R.|last3=Fitter|first3=A|year=2003|title=Wild flowers of Britain and Ireland: The Complete Guide to the British and Irish Flora.|publisher=A & C Black|location=London|isbn=978-1408179505|pages=150}}</ref>

The species is native to Europe from Britain to the Caucasus.<ref name="nrmse">{{cite web|url=http://linnaeus.nrm.se/flora/di/faba/trifo/trifmedv.jpg|title=Trifolium medium|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20060717024423/http://linnaeus.nrm.se/flora/di/faba/trifo/trifmedv.jpg|archive-date=2006-07-17}}</ref>

